# A set: a collection of distinct things considered as one thing, the bottom of the mathematical foundation. Everything
# else is built from sets: a function is a set of pairs, a number is a set, a structure is a set with operations. The
# only relation a bare set carries is membership, whether a thing is in it. The form carries an opaque membership; the
# axioms (extensionality, that two sets with the same members are equal, and the rest of the set-theoretic axioms) live
# in the set-theory files.
form set
  link member, note private
